<title>UK: TABLE-Unilever H1 earnings rise.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Unilever H1 earnings rise.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three months to June 30, 1997</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		134.43	  vs 19.39</p>
<p> Net profit		 2,948	   vs 360</p>
<p> Pretax		     3,858	   vs 609</p>
<p> Turnover		   8,830	   vs 8,710</p>
<p> Operating profit	 887	     vs 674</p>
<p>NOTE - Pretax figure includes 3.022 bln stg profit on specialty chemicals  sale to Imperial Chemical Industries Plc for $8.0 billion. The figures  are at constant rates of exchange.</p>
<p>		 - Six months to June 30, 1997</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		150.19	   vs 36.50</p>
<p> Net profit		 3,328	    vs 705</p>
<p> Pretax		     4,396	    vs 1,112</p>
<p> Turnover		   16,818	   vs 16,314</p>
<p> Operating profit	 1,472	    vs 1,231</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts had forecast H1 pre-tax profits in a range between  720 and 780 million stg. Full company name is Unilever. --London Newsroom  +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
